# Code_Aster Command File - Generated by MecwayAsterBridge
# Template for the thermal -> mechanical chain (welding: residual stress and
# distortion; Mecway T31 with a Thermal stress): first THER_LINEAIRE /
# THER_NON_LINE as in AsterTemplate_Thermique.comm (bridge_thermal.py),
# then STAT_NON_LINE with the temperature as command variable
# (AFFE_VARC NOM_VARC='TEMP', EVOL = the thermal result;
# bridge_thermomech.py). Syntax source: test case hsnv100e (Code-Aster 17.4).
#
# Temperatures are in degrees CELSIUS (see the thermal template);
# so are VALE_REF and the material functions of TEMP.
#
# Placeholders (name between single braces):
#   thermal: defigroup_block, model_block, materials_block,
#     fieldmat_block, funcs_block, listinst_block, loads_block, solve_block,
#     calc_champ_block (see AsterTemplate_Thermique.comm)
#   mechanical (bridge_thermomech.build_blocks):
#     mech_defigroup_block  -> res_ther = res (thermal result), DEFI_GROUP
#                              for the boundary conditions, possibly LINE_QUAD +
#                              PROJ_CHAMP of the temperature
#     mech_model_block      -> AFFE_MODELE (MECANIQUE)
#     mech_materials_block  -> DEFI_FONCTION/DEFI_CONSTANTE of TEMP,
#                              DEFI_MATERIAU (ELAS or ELAS_FO, ECRO_LINE(_FO)
#                              or TRACTION)
#     mech_fieldmat_block   -> AFFE_MATERIAU with AFFE_VARC TEMP
#     mech_loads_block      -> AFFE_CHAR_MECA(_F) + DEFI_LIST_INST
#     mech_solve_block      -> STAT_NON_LINE
#     mech_calc_champ_block -> CALC_CHAMP (stresses, plastic strain) and the
#                              summary BRIDGE_THERMOMECA
#   export_block            -> aster_results_export (res = mechanical,
#                              res_ther / res_flux = thermal)
#   med_block               -> MED (setting med_export)
#
# A brace that is not a placeholder: double it ({{ or }}).

